WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.017
The anchor selects top-level employees with no manager.

00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:10.522
The recursive term joins employees to the current organization result when an employee's manager ID matches a

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:12.557
current employee ID. Depth increases by one.

00:00:12.557 --> 00:00:14.657
Path appends the employee name.

00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:18.832
Run the query and inspect how the hierarchy expands level by level.

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:23.367
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:29.022
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:31.267
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:37.247
In a real setting such as an operations team comparing each event with the previous and next event,

00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:42.842
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.237
before discussing syntax.

00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:49.990
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
